{% set pageTitle = "Free Pilot Logbook, No Subscription — Open Source | NinerLog" %}
{% set pageDescription = "A pilot logbook that is genuinely free: no subscription, no tiers, no ads, no expiring trial. Open source, donation-funded, and your data exports anytime." %}
{% set pagePath = "/free-pilot-logbook" %}
{% set sitemapChangefreq = "monthly" %}
{% set sitemapPriority = "0.9" %}
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="relative bg-linear-to-br from-navy-900 via-navy-800 to-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-topo-pattern pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 text-center relative z-10">
    <div class="mb-4 reveal">
      <span class="freq-badge">
        <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-blink"></span>
        NO SUBSCRIPTION &bull; NO TIERS &bull; NO ADS
      </span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white text-balance reveal reveal-delay-1">
      Free Pilot Logbook, No Subscription
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal reveal-delay-2">
      Not free-for-30-days. Not free until you hit 50 flights. Not free with the export button greyed out. Free.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-px bg-linear-to-r from-transparent via-sky-500/20 to-transparent" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     WHAT FREE MEANS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-6 reveal">
      What &ldquo;free&rdquo; means here.
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <p>
        &ldquo;Free&rdquo; has been stretched thin by software that is free in the way a first taste is free. So it is worth being specific about what it means for NinerLog:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>There is one tier</strong>, and you are on it. No pro plan, no unlock, no feature held back as an upsell.</li>
        <li><strong>No flight limit.</strong> Log twelve hours a year or twelve hundred; it makes no difference.</li>
        <li><strong>No ads, and nothing sold on.</strong> Your logbook is not an advertising surface and your data is not a product.</li>
        <li><strong>Export is not a paid feature.</strong> CSV, PDF and JSON, whenever you want, in full.</li>
        <li><strong>No credit card</strong> to sign up, so there is nothing to cancel later.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The uncomfortable question that follows is the obvious one, so here is the answer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     HOW IT'S FUNDED
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-6 reveal">
      So how is it paid for?
    </h2>
    <div class="prose prose-slate prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none reveal reveal-delay-1">
      <p>
        NinerLog is built by one person &mdash; a software engineer who has been flying GA since 2018 &mdash; and it is deliberately cheap to run. Hosting, database, domain and certificates come to roughly <strong>$30 a month</strong>. Development is volunteer time.
      </p>
      <p>
        That bill is covered by <a href="/donate">donations from pilots who use it</a>. There is no venture capital behind this, which means there is no investor who will eventually need the free tier to start converting. That pressure is the usual reason a free logbook stops being free, and it simply does not exist here.
      </p>
      <p>
        Donating is genuinely optional. Nothing is withheld from people who do not, and there is no badge, no tier, no nag screen. If NinerLog saves you from a paper logbook, that is already the point of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     WHY YOU CAN BELIEVE IT
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-12 lg:mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white reveal">
        Why this promise is worth more than a promise.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto reveal reveal-delay-1">
        Every logbook says it cares about your data. Open source is what makes it checkable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">The licence protects you</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The API is AGPL-3.0, everything else MIT. Today&rsquo;s code cannot be retroactively taken away &mdash; if NinerLog ever changed direction, the version you trusted stays forkable by anyone.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-2">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">You can leave at any time</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The exit is built in and tested, not a formality. Take a full CSV, PDF or JSON export and go &mdash; lock-in is the problem NinerLog was written to solve in the first place.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="group p-6 bg-white dark:bg-navy-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-navy-700 rounded-xl hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-1 transition-all duration-200 reveal reveal-delay-3">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-2">Or take the whole thing</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          If the hosted service ever stopped, you could <a href="/self-hosted" class="text-sky-500 hover:text-sky-400">run it on your own server</a> with Docker Compose. Your logbook outlives the project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     HONEST NOTE
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="p-6 lg:p-8 bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-xl reveal">
      <h2 class="text-xl lg:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-800 dark:text-white mb-4">
        The honest trade-off.
      </h2>
      <div class="prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <p class="mb-0">
          Free and solo-built has a cost, and it is fair to say it out loud: NinerLog is younger than the commercial logbooks, there is no support desk, and features arrive when one person has evenings free. Some paid apps are more polished and more automated, and for some pilots that is worth paying for. What you get in exchange here is a logbook that cannot be taken hostage &mdash; and the ability to
          <a href="https://github.com/fjaeckel/ninerlog" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">check every word of this</a>
          against the source.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     CTA
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="bg-navy-900 py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white mb-6 reveal">
      No trial. Just the logbook.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 reveal reveal-delay-1">
      Sign up with an email address and start logging. That is the whole funnel.
    </p>
    <a href="https://app.ninerlog.com/register"
       class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-4 bg-linear-to-r from-amber-400 to-amber-500 text-navy-900 font-semibold text-lg rounded-full shadow-lg shadow-amber-400/30 hover:shadow-xl hover:shadow-amber-400/40 hover:scale-[1.02] active:scale-[0.98] transition-all duration-200 focus-visible:outline-hidden focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-amber-400 focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-navy-900 reveal reveal-delay-2">
      Start Logging &mdash; It&rsquo;s Free
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
